WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.150
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.570
Welcome.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.540
Thank you.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.320
Please sit wherever you'd like.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.980
Welcome.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.660
I see you've come again.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.020
The pale-faced diviner from the Land of Sea!

00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:00.230
Well, well, if it isn't the mountain ape 
whose only talent is swinging a sword.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:05.600
Forgive me. I meant the samurai 
from the Land of Mountains.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.690
Hmph! You are as insufferable as ever.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.230
Why are you always here 
at the same time as me?

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.240
I could ask the same thing of you.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:20.170
I am, after all, quite busy in my 
position as the court diviner.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.240
This is the only time 
I am able to come here.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.740
On the other hand...

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.210
You are little more than a court guard,

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:32.110
so you are free to come whenever you want.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.250
A guard, you say?!

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.250
You're no more than a sham fortune-teller!

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.010
Excuse me?!

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.250
Will they be all right?

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.020
They're always like that.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.310
Mm, that's good!

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.320
Anyway, you can't blame them.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.150
The countries they both come from 
probably play a part in it.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.390
Their countries?

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.440
Oh, you didn't know?

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:01.250
Souemon's Land of Mountains 
and Doushun's Land of Sea

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.030
are neighboring countries 
that are always at odds.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:09.460
It's no surprise that the two of them 
start fighting at the drop of a hat.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.670
I had no idea...

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:18.130
Oh, but what if they just came here 
at different times of the day?

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:22.270
They probably both feel like caving on 
that point would mean admitting defeat.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.430
Huh?

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.710
What did you say?

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:25.500
What's the matter?

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.740
I-I should really go and stop them!

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.070
Off you go, then.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:32.690
K-Kuro-san! Why are you 
just watching them fight?!

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.190
Please try to stop them!

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:39.170
I sense no murderous intent,
so I believe they should be fine.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:43.050
B-But they'll disturb the other customers!

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:46.950
You're just covering it up with that 
shady act and the stench of the sea!

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.330
Well, the only impressive 
thing about you is your howl.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.960
Sirs...

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.480
I apologize for all the noise.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.370
I am terribly sorry.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.100
It's all right.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.750
E-Excuse me...

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:12.200
If you stay so close to the entrance, 
you'll block other customers.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.090
Please have a seat wherever you'd like.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.500
She does have a point.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.120
Yes, indeed.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.640
What?!

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.360
They're sitting together?!

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.370
Here are your complimentary 
glasses of water and wet hand towels.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:29.840
Thank you.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.230
I'd like to order now.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:34.620
Oh... Of course!

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.220
Thank you for waiting. 
What can I get for you?

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:41.900
I would like okonomiyaki with pork and egg.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.510
With plenty of sauce!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.870
I would like okonomiyaki, too.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.260
With plenty of seafood and bonito flakes.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.430
Coming right up!

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.310
Seafood as usual, eh?

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.940
You should be sick of that, 
as a man from the Land of Sea!

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:01.750
Well, I would hardly expect pork to be 
uncommon in the Land of Mountains, either.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.910
Two orders of okonomiyaki, one with 
pork and egg, one with seafood.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:14.750
Lots of sauce on the pork and egg, 
and lots of bonito flakes on the seafood.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:15.850
Got it.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:17.390
Um, Master...

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:18.580
What is it?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:22.370
Souemon-san and Doushun-san 
get along so terribly.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.960
Why did they sit at the same table?

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.590
I'm just so anxious that they 
might start fighting again.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:30.410
Hmm...

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.600
They should be fine.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.670
Huh?

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:36.130
I don't think they actually 
get along poorly.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.960
You don't?

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.970
If they can eat a meal at the same table,

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:43.630
they must share some kind of mutual respect.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:46.020
Mutual... respect?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.870
They say the more you fight, 
the closer you are.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.620
They fight, but... they're close?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:57.500
I think you'll understand if you watch them.

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:00.110
The more you fight, the closer you are?

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.820
Mutual respect?

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.680
I don't understand it.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:10.070
Oh? So the Land of Sea will be doing 
more business with the Empire?

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:14.650
Yes, and it is expected to bring even 
more wealth to the Land of Sea.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.640
And I hear your country has joined 
forces with a dwarf weaponsmith.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.770
I guess a diviner from the Land of Sea
 must have keen ears, eh?

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:26.270
I only heard a rumor carried on the breeze.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:29.280
And what are the dwarven weapons like?

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.730
They're outstandingly well-made!

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:34.000
Swords and axes imbued with mana,

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.850
armor that can even repel magic...

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.690
And every single one is 
of the finest quality!

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:42.040
Oh? How very intriguing!

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.430
Thank you for waiting.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:53.550
<i>Okonomiyaki</i>

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.550
Your okonomiyaki.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:59.950
That audibly sizzling hot plate!

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:02.560
The scent of the sauce 
that piques my appetite!

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.540
One would never imagine that the
elegantly-swaying bonito flakes,

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:10.570
which look so much like wood shavings, 
would smell so vividly of the sea!

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.890
I've waited seven long days for this!

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:13.730
Indeed!

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:15.950
Now, let's eat!

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:15.950
Let us eat!

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:27.700
<i>The scents of sauce and bonito 
flakes fill my mouth.</i>

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.090
<i>The batter is crispy and 
savory on the surface,</i>

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.840
<i>but soft and fluffy on the inside!</i>

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:35.650
<i>The light sprinkling of powdered seaweed,</i>

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:39.330
<i>the bonito flakes that look like wood 
shavings from a carpenter's plane...</i>

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:44.260
<i>The sweet and salty sauce, and the 
mellow sourness of the mayonnaise...</i>

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:47.340
<i>The sweetness of the shredded cabbage and</i>

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.000
<i>the savoriness of the 
meat hit me all at once!</i>

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.110
<i>Now this is what I call okonomiyaki!</i>

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:53.330
<i>Irresistible!</i>

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:56.620
<i>My goodness.</i>

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.490
<i>I see the samurai from the Land of Mountains</i>

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.130
<i>still has utterly abhorrent eating habits.</i>

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:06.110
<i>One should be more elegant 
when partaking of a meal.</i>

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.780
<i>It truly is delicious!</i>

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.950
<i>The shripe and krakeen, 
cut into bite-sized pieces,</i>

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:17.130
<i>have been handled so well that 
there's no unpleasant odor at all!</i>

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:20.150
<i>The tender-yet-springy texture 
and the savory flavor</i>

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:22.640
<i>truly make it a dish of elegant taste!</i>

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.470
<i>If he keeps eating it that slowly,</i>

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:32.900
<i>this piping-hot okonomiyaki will get cold.</i>

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.810
Just one really doesn't seem like enough.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:48.670
I agree.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.420
Perhaps I'll order another.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:55.590
I shall do the same.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.770
Seconds, please!

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.100
Sure.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.260
I would also like seconds.

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:02.790
Both okonomiyaki, right?

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:05.350
Would you like the same flavors again?

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:08.630
I'll take the seafood...

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:10.860
And I would like pork and egg.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:11.980
Huh?

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.220
C-Coming right up.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.070
You saw me enjoying the pork and egg so much

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:21.490
that it made you want to try it as well, eh?

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.860
What about you?

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:27.250
You saw me eating so elegantly that it 
made you want to try the seafood, yes?

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:29.770
There you go being stubborn again.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:31.390
You're not being honest!

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:34.760
You have not been honest, either.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.900
The seafood is delicious, too!

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:49.610
The taste of the sea goes just 
as splendidly with the sauce!

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:54.260
And the tenderness of the shripe gives it 
an appeal that the pork and egg lacks!

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:58.000
Yes, exactly! I knew you would understand!

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.160
Indeed! And what do you 
think of the pork and egg?

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.160
It's delicious!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:07.130
Sweet oils from the mild-smelling 
meat have soaked into the batter.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.920
It's a very rich flavor!

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.420
I could eat these one after another!

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.150
There, you see?

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:18.460
What do they cook, and how, 
to result in this flavor?

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.660
If we could find out and learn to make it,

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:24.180
do you not agree that it would aid the 
growth of our countries even further?

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.900
No doubt about that!

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.600
It may be even better if we use

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:35.190
ingredients from my Land of Mountains
 and your Land of Sea!

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:38.200
That is a brilliant idea!

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.950
It's hard to believe they 
were fighting earlier.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:46.210
Is this the "mutual respect" 
that Master spoke of?

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:47.950
Is it?

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.460
I envy them a bit.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:54.960
Me, too!

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.980
See? I told you they'd be fine.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.690
We're done cleaning up!

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:05.700
All done.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.680
Great, thanks.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.250
Master, what are you doing?

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.810
I'm making a dessert called "shaved ice."

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.410
It's getting hotter lately,

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.240
so I thought I'd start serving 
it as a seasonal special.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:24.200
It's so sparkly and pretty!

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:26.670
There's still some time before we open.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:27.940
Would you like to taste it?

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:29.960
Can I?!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.210
You, too, Kuro.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:33.470
Very well.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.960
Which color syrup would you like?

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:42.260
Um... Which one should I get?

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.970
Oh, I'll take red!

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.380
Got it. Kuro?

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.410
Any of them.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.380
Okay, Aletta-san, pick one for her.

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:51.420
Huh?

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.720
Um, okay... then...

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:55.260
Blue!

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:55.980
Okay.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:10.760
Thank you, god of demons, 
for this, my daily bread.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.070
Now, let's eat!

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:15.290
Let's eat.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.400
It's cold.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:25.300
But it's also sweet and delicious!

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:28.430
When it enters my mouth, it melts away.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:34.390
My head hurts!

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:35.860
Is it a curse?

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:38.030
It's not a curse.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:40.960
Eating this can cause that. It's harmless.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:43.320
How intimidating...

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.900
My head suddenly hurts, but...

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:47.820
It's delicious!

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.700
Oh! Kuro-san, your mouth is all blue!

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.910
Your tongue is red, too.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.410
Really?!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.540
The coloring in the syrup sticks to you.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.160
Oh, I see!

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:03.170
Interesting.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:07.840
That's one of the fun parts 
of eating shaved ice.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:15.900
Oh, is that a customer?

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.610
I'll take this one.

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:24.610
<b>Paradise</b>

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.590
I'm so bored.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:39.150
There's nothing to do.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:45.940
Even if it was to escape the epidemic 
that struck the elves so long ago,

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:51.220
turning this area into a floating 
island was going way too far.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:55.460
Then again, it's because 
they fled to the sky

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:58.980
that I was born and can live here today...

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:03.980
But I've even grown bored with the magic 
research that my parents left behind.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.740
What should I do today?

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:15.000
Something's odd about the flow of mana.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.950
Maybe today won't be just an ordinary day!

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:26.100
Golem, take me to the destination.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.150
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.150
Oh? What's this?

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:46.260
Teleportation magic?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.650
And it connects to another world.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:52.250
This should be interesting.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:01.960
Huh, look at this.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.010
It really is another world.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.730
Welcome!

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:11.040
What is this? What does it do?

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.040
Uh, excuse me...

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:14.490
Who are you?

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:19.100
You have short ears... 
and horns on your head.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:23.870
A descendant of the ones who prayed to 
the God of Chaos, Ruler of All Life?

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:25.520
I've never seen one before.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:28.610
Huh? Life? Chaos?

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:31.610
Oh, I guess it'd be clearer 
if I said "demons."

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:33.370
Wait, you...

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.490
Your tongue is so red!

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.710
Is that true of all demons?

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:40.960
My tongue is red because 
I just ate shaved ice.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.620
Let me have a look!

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:45.130
Please stop that.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.730
Oh... I apologize.

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:50.540
I haven't interacted with 
anyone else in 200 years,

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:52.250
so I got a bit excited.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:54.260
Oh, it's all right...

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.220
Wait, 200 years?!

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:00.000
Yes. I live alone on an island in 
the sky that has no correspondence

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.020
with the surface folks.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:05.640
Also, this is the first time I've 
left the island in my entire life.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:08.060
A floating island?

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:11.400
Yes, using special magic 
that my parents created.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:12.720
Wow...

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:15.340
Anyway, what is this place?

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:18.340
This is a shop called Nekoya 
that serves cuisine.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:19.160
A shop?

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:24.900
A shop is a thing that offers goods 
in exchange for currency, right?

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:25.920
Correct.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:29.860
And "cuisine" refers to things like 
meat and vegetables that have been

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.390
boiled, baked, or otherwise prepared 
to make them taste good, right?

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:33.430
Correct.

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:37.430
How interesting! Serve me 
some of this "cuisine"!

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.930
Of course. Please sit anywhere you'd like.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.930
Here's your complimentary 
water and wet hand towel.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.760
Can you read the language 
of the Eastern Continent?

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:49.090
Not a problem.

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:51.210
Then here's a menu.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.230
I'm not sure what to make of this "cuisine."

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:00.590
Serve me something unusual, please.

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:04.460
Something made without milk, meat, 
fish, or anything like that.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.020
Something... unusual?

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.560
Oh, I know! May I see that menu, please?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.470
How about one of these?

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:17.020
We just began serving them 
today as a seasonal special.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.270
A seasonal special?

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:23.980
Then I'll have this thing called 
"green tea shaved ice."

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.580
Coming right up!

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.450
This is refreshing and delicious!

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:34.240
Oh...

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:38.240
This water has citrus juice in it.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:41.870
What in the world are these?

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:48.140
It's salty.

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:52.630
Could this be what they call "salt"? 
I've never tasted it before!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.160
Yes, that is salt.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:57.540
There is also sugar and soy sauce.

00:17:57.540 --> 00:18:01.140
Soy sauce? I've never heard of that.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:05.210
Ah, so this is sugar, eh?

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:08.510
The green tea shaved ice 
is made with it, too.

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:11.130
Then I'll look forward 
to tasting it that way.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:15.140
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:18.660
<i>Green Tea Shaved Ice</i>

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.660
Here's your green tea shaved ice.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:22.360
Huh... So this is "cuisine"?

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:24.660
It's cold.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:27.910
Is this the thing they call "snow"?

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:32.590
It looks like I'm supposed 
to use this to eat it.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:34.780
Okay, I'll try it.

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.160
This is delicious!

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:43.420
It melts quickly in my mouth,

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:46.970
and it has a refreshing aroma and a hint 
of bitterness that enhances the sweetness!

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:48.810
I could get hooked on this!

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:52.400
<i>But what is this grass-colored liquid?</i>

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:55.320
<i>It looks like the syrup made 
by boiling medicinal herbs,</i>

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:59.910
<i>but how long was it boiled to achieve 
such a rich, dark shade of green?</i>

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:08.730
<i>What is this intense pain that 
feels like it's piercing my head?!</i>

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:18.370
That pain happens when you eat too much?

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:23.700
Well, it goes away on its own 
quickly enough, so it's not a problem.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:27.020
Now, I think I'll try these beans next.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:33.210
<i>They're sweet! Is this what happens to beans 
that are boiled until they dissolve?!</i>

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:34.940
<i>No...</i>

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:38.190
<i>They must have been boiled with sugar.</i>

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:41.070
<i>I have beans in my medicinal 
herb garden that look similar,</i>

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:43.950
<i>but they're hard and not fit for eating.</i>

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:47.500
<i>But when they're boiled 
with sugar like this...</i>

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:51.250
<i>They're so soft and sweet!</i>

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:55.170
<i>Now, this is next.</i>

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.770
Just what is this, anyway?

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:05.950
<i>A unique texture... soft, but also springy.</i>

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:10.140
<i>It tastes faintly of the beans 
and the grass-colored snow,</i>

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.890
<i>but it doesn't seem to have 
any flavor of its own.</i>

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:16.830
<i>Just what is the purpose 
of these white balls?</i>

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.110
<i>Wait, could it be...</i>

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.200
<i>Oh! Now I get it!</i>

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:31.030
<i>The light crunch of the 
half-melted grass-colored snow,</i>

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:34.140
<i>the sweetness of the beans, and the 
springiness of the white balls...</i>

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:36.500
<i>Eating them together softens the 
bitterness of the green syrup,</i>

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.740
<i>enhances the sweetness,</i>

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:42.220
<i>and holds the flavors in my mouth much 
longer than when they're eaten separately!</i>

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.090
<i>Magnificent!</i>

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:47.120
<i>So this is what "cuisine" is!</i>

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:52.600
<i>Why did I never take any interest 
in something so intriguing before?!</i>

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:55.790
I want to beat up my younger self!

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:58.960
I have a question!

00:20:58.960 --> 00:20:59.610
Okay.

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:01.750
What is it?

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:04.210
Can I come here at any time?

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:06.610
No, only once every seven days.

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:07.870
I see...

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:13.750
I'd like one more just like this, please.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:16.140
Sure, coming right up!

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:17.840
Oh, also...

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:26.630
I guess it's no wonder I feel 
cold after eating four bowls.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:27.640
Still...

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:31.090
I can't believe he shared this much with me!

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:38.650
Now, I wonder if I can reproduce that 
green tea shaved ice somehow.

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:41.540
I should be able to make 
the snow part by using the

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:44.110
blizzard spell I learned from Mom.

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:49.160
The issues are the medicinal herb 
syrup and the springy white balls.

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:51.160
For starters...

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:56.400
To my medicinal herb garden!

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:01.290
I'm sure it'll have something I can use!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:42.560
<i>Roast Beef</i>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:42.560
<i>Roast Beef</i>

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Cheesecake Again</i>

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Cheesecake Again</i>
